  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n   \u2022 Central idea: Use finite-difference gradient approximation within a smarter optimization framework.\n   \u2022 Motivation: Gradient-based SLSQP method was shown to converge faster (within 50-100 iterations) than previous implementation but needs more careful initialization and constraint satisfaction.\n   \u2022 Bottleneck addressed: Current implementation uses linear projection to satisfy integral constraint, but random trials often fail to find good starting points. We address this by combining multiple initialization strategies (interleaved, interpolated initial pattern, and uniform random with projection).\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   \u2022 Variables: Discrete step function h \u2208 [0,1]^n with \u2211(h_dx)=1 (dx=2/n)\n   \u2022 Objective: C5 = (max_k \u222b(h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx) * (2/n)/dx\n   \u2022 Constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i, \u2211h = n/2 (because \u2211h*dx=1)\n   \u2022 Objective computation: Compute finite correlation using np.correlate(mode='full'), scale by dx\n   \u2022 Optimization method: SLSQP with analytic gradients for improved convergence\n   \u2022 Key changes: \n     \u2022 Use fixpoint iteration to maintain constraint satisfaction during optimization\n     \u2022 Implement integral constraint more robustly as a single equality constraint\n     \u2022 Use h_n = projection_onto_simplex to ensure h[i]\u2208{0,1} if feasible\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n   \u2022 Data structures:\n     \u2022 hnumpy array of length n\n     \u2022 n_points for [0,2] space\n     \u2022 dx = 2.0 / n_points\n   \u2022 Steps:\n     1. Read initial_h_values if available\n     2. Validate candidate:\n        a. Check 0<=h[i]<=1\n        b. Sum = n/2 (allow small error)\n     3. Implement objective:\n        i. corr = correlate(h,1-h,mode='full')\n        ii. objective = dx * np.max(corr)\n     4. Gradient computation:\n        i. Find lag k that maximizes correlation\n        ii. Compute gradient for h as finite differences\n     5. Optimization:\n        i. Setup bounds (0,1) per variable\n        ii. Problem with equality constraint (sum h = n/2)\n     6. Updates:\n        \u2022 Refine parent construction parameters\n        \u2022 Add constraint satisfaction checks\n        \u2022 Incorporate objective evaluation at correct scales\n\n4. Search choices:\n   \u2022 Default parameters:\n     - n_points = 151 (smallest integer satisfying constraint exactly)\n     - Optimization iterations = 50\n     - Random candidate attempts = 15\n     - Interleaved candidate attempts = 20\n     - Refine parent features:\n        \u2207grid_spacing = 0.05, max_perturbations = 100\n   \u2022 Variation rules:\n     * When stuck: add 0.01 to dx_parent, recompute n_points\n     * Blend initial pattern with random trials...\n     * Animate repair procedures\n\n5. Compute budget:\n   \u2022 Core lemma SLSQP runs 0.1-0.5 seconds per point (n_points)\n   \u2022 15 trials * 50 iterations \u2248 150 seconds\n   \u2022 Memory: 15*n_elements floats\n   \u2022 Stopping: Monitor time usage during SLSQP\n     * 100ms: adjust hyperparameters\n     * 80% complete: switch to exploitation mode\n\n6. Validation:\n   \u2022 Post-optimization checking:\n     a. Re-project to satisfy integral constraint\n     b. Recompute objective to verify\n     c. Check 0<=values<=1 to required precision\n   \u2022 Failure cases:\n     * Infeasibility: repair by projection\n     * Objective overflow: switch to log scale",
